  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This pastitsio serves 6 and takes 30 minutes of preparation plus 55 minutes in the oven. A spiced beef and tomato layer sits beneath a thick, set bechamel that forms a golden crust on top. This version uses bulgur wheat as the grain base in place of traditional tube pasta."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make the meat sauce first and let it cool slightly before assembling. A hot meat sauce can cause the bechamel to slip when you pour it over. The assembled dish can be refrigerated unbaked for up to a day, which makes it a good choice when you need to prepare ahead."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
