      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ""
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "pastitsio-term"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Pastitsio"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is Sunday lunch food across Greece, the kind of dish that families make in large quantities and eat across several days. The cinnamon in the meat sauce is the hallmark of Greek spiced mince and separates it clearly from Italian-style ragus. It reheats well in a moderate oven covered with foil. Leftovers are arguably better the day after baking once the layers have fully set."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
